CRASH-18: reject EN_addrule lines that do not fit the line buffer

EN_addrule copies each line of the rule text into char line2[MAXLINE+1]
with strcpy and then appends a newline, so any line of MAXLINE (1,024)
characters or more overflowed the stack. EN_addrule now returns error
214 (too many characters in input line) for such a line, the same limit
that applies to a line of an input file.

Apply from the root of an EPANET checkout at 83e25bb:
    git apply CRASH-18_fix.patch

diff --git a/src/epanet.c b/src/epanet.c
index 47dc1e4..2c5a115 100644
--- a/src/epanet.c
+++ b/src/epanet.c
@@ -5648,6 +5648,13 @@ int DLLEXPORT EN_addrule(EN_Project p, char *rule)
         nextline = strchr(line, '\n');
         if (nextline) *nextline = '\0';
 
+        // The line and the newline added below must fit in line2
+        if (strlen(line) >= MAXLINE)
+        {
+            rules->Errcode = 214;
+            break;
+        }
+
         // Copy and tokenize the current line
         strcpy(line2, line);
         strcat(line2, "\n");  // Tokenizer won't work without this
